<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sumana Thera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Phra Sumana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sumana Thera was a Buddhist monk from Sukhothai who, at the invitation of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kue-na">Kue Na</a>, came to Chiang Mai in 1369. He established there a monastic ordination lineage derived from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, based at the new monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wat-suan-dok">Wat Suan Dok</a>, and tradition credits him with enshrining the relic of Doi Suthep.</p></div>
